WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.900
Every lesson starts with a real question
about the data, and ends with

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.500
you answering it.

3
00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:11.140
Here, you learn one idea at a time and put
it to work straight away:

4
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:16.620
first you read a short explanation with a
worked example, then you fill the gaps in

5
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.420
code that's already started, then you fix
a mistake and watch what changes,

6
00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:25.880
and finally you write the code yourself,
using everything you've practised.

7
00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.140
The task stays beside your editor while
you work, so you can run your code to see

8
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.700
its output, submit your answer for instant
feedback on what to check next,

9
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.400
and use that feedback to revise and try
again, opening one hint at a time

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.200
whenever you need a nudge.

11
00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:47.300
Step-through diagrams let you follow the
code as the table changes, and you can go

12
00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.920
back to compare any step with the one
before it.

13
00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.120
It all runs in your browser with nothing
to install;

14
00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:58.120
the free R courses are open now, and SQL
and Python are coming in December,

15
00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.460
so start your first lesson today.
